orcshot (0.1.0-5) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fix save_image_to_file always building an RGBA (has_alpha=True)
    pixbuf regardless of target format. JPEG has no alpha channel -
    Ubuntu 24.04's older GdkPixbuf JPEG backend silently discarded it,
    but 26.04's newer glycin-based one rejects an RGBA-flagged pixbuf
    outright ("does not support the color type Rgba8"). Confirmed as
    the real cause of 0.1.0-4's resolute build failure via the actual
    Launchpad buildlog. save_image_to_file now composites onto white
    and builds a genuine 3-channel, has_alpha=False pixbuf for JPEG
    specifically.

 -- Orcshot <314918217+artificialorctelligence@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 22 Aug 2026 13:45:05 -0500

orcshot (0.1.0-4) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Add gir1.2-gsound-1.0 to Build-Depends. Missing since task #158 added
    it as a runtime Depends only - the test suite (run during the build
    via dh_auto_test) imports capture/capture_feedback.py, which calls
    gi.require_version("GSound", "1.0") at module load time, so a clean
    build chroot without this typelib fails to even collect
    tests/unit/capture/test_capture_feedback.py. Confirmed as the exact
    cause of 0.1.0-3's real build failure on Launchpad's amd64 builder
    (buildlog: "ValueError: Namespace GSound not available"). Not caught
    locally because this dev machine already had gir1.2-gsound-1.0
    installed from earlier testing.

 -- Orcshot <314918217+artificialorctelligence@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 22 Aug 2026 12:51:23 -0500

